=== p2-windows · W7 · page:charging/Powershare (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:charging/Powershare   kind=page   web route=/powershare
Web source  : web/src/features/charging/pages/PowersharePage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/PowersharePage/{PowersharePage.Model.cs, .Source.cs, .ViewModel.cs, .cs}
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent UserControl view), exactly as the
  sibling W7 EnergyFlowPage / BatteryDegradationPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "PowersharePage.xaml +
  PowersharePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Charging" is mapped onto these real conventions. The surface
  registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("Powershare", already in
  TeslaSync.App.Core/Navigation/RouteTable.cs L261 → /powershare, group Charging) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useSignalObservations (GET /signals/observations). The web
  page reads FIVE cold Powershare signals from signal_observations (PowershareStatus, PowershareType,
  PowershareStopReason, PowershareHoursLeft, PowershareInstantaneousPowerKW), one useSignalObservations hook each.
  PowershareClientFeed (PowersharePage.Source.cs) fans these out to five independent reads of the generated
  operation id get_api_v1_signals_observations (resolved against the generated endpoint table, ApiEndpoints.cs
  L407 — asserted by ClientFeed_operation_resolves_against_the_generated_endpoint_table), each scoped by
  vehicle_id + field + limit=1, exactly as the sibling AutopilotSectionSource references the same endpoint. Each
  read is best-effort and independent (web parity: a failed/empty hook just leaves that value absent), folded into
  a PowershareReading via the tolerant PowershareObservation reducers (the native port of latestText/latestNumeric
  + adaptObservations' value-kind discriminator, tolerating snake_case + camelCase keys). The default
  PowersharePage() ctor uses EmptyPowershareFeed (the no-data empty state), mirroring EnergyFlowPage; the client
  feed is exercised by tests (ClientFeed_sends_five_observation_reads_with_vehicle_field_and_limit). No HTTP
  touches the view.
- The web page renders its states INSIDE the PageContainer body and ALWAYS shows both GlassPanels, so the native
  port reproduces them as visible Fluent regions per ADR-006: the page header (PageTitle + Subhead) is always
  shown; loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(3) + TsSkeleton shimmer; error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) +
  Retry; and the two-panel content layout is shown in BOTH the empty AND success states. GlassPanel1 always
  carries its "Powershare Status" header + status badge and swaps its body between the three stat cards (success)
  and a TsEmptyState ("No Powershare data received yet…"); GlassPanel5 always carries its "Stop Reason" header and
  swaps its body between the stop-reason chip + help text and a TsEmptyState ("No stop reason recorded…"). Never a
  blank region.
- Badge variants (web statusVariant / stopReasonVariant) are ported verbatim into PowershareProjection,
  preserving the web's exact substring-precedence — including the documented quirk that "inactive" matches the
  includes('active') success branch first (test Status_variant_reproduces_web_inactive_quirk). Web BadgeVariant ->
  StatusKind: success→Success, danger→Danger, neutral→Neutral, warning→Warning.
- Units (ADR-002): the two numeric readouts are NOT unit-system dependent and the web applies no conversion —
  PowershareInstantaneousPowerKW is rendered with a literal "kW" suffix and PowershareHoursLeft with "h". The
  native port formats them at the display boundary through the shared ScalarFormatters.FormatNumber (web
  fmtNumber: power @2dp "12.34 kW", hours @1dp "2.5 h"), never storing/computing a non-SI value. There is no
  miles/mph/psi/°F path on this page.
- i18n (ADR-014): all 14 manifest keys flow through ILocalizer.GetString("<web key>", "<English default>") in
  PowershareProjection, resolved UNCONDITIONALLY at the top of Project so every key is recorded in every data
  state (tests Projection_resolves_every_required_string_key + _even_in_the_loading_state + _even_when_data_is_
  absent). 9 of the 14 keys already existed in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw; the 5 missing keys
  (powershare.hoursLeftSub, .noData, .noStopReason, .stopReasonHelp, .subtitle) were added verbatim (web key
  names, "translation.<key>") to all three catalogs in alphabetical position within the existing powershare
  block, preserving LF/UTF-8-no-BOM (validated: 14/14 present, valid XML, no CR, no BOM in each catalog). NOTE:
  the resw is generator-owned and sources from web en.json; these 5 hand-added keys would not be re-emitted by
  gen-i18n until the same keys land in web en.json — documented here, not silent. The resw is not part of the
  dotnet build, so this does not affect the build gate.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties.SetName on the page, both panels, the status/stop badges, the three stat
  cards, and the error/empty surfaces; the view exposes a Group AutomationPeer that falls back to the page title.
  Light/dark + tokens honored — every colour/typography comes from the W1/W2 design tokens via the shared
  components (TsGlassPanel/TsBadge/TsStatCard/TsEmptyState/PageTitle/Subhead/PanelTitle), and the section icons are
  tinted from the themed StatusResources accent brushes (warning/danger).
- Predecessor repair (no red shipped, no silent drift): the W4 shell file
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs was committed in a merge-corrupted state on this
  integration branch — the YearReview (L90) and AutomationList (L96) PageFactory.Register lambdas were each
  missing their closing `return page; });` (a .gitattributes merge=union concatenation hazard), which broke the
  whole TeslaSync.App C# compile (CS1026/CS1002/CS1513 at L140) and cascaded into ~84 spurious XamlCompiler
  WMC0001/WMC0110 "Unknown type" errors + a WMC9999 internal error. Both lambdas were repaired to mirror the
  adjacent (correct) Automations lambda, then the Powershare registration was appended. This is the single file
  the W7 surface must edit to register itself, so the fix is in-scope; it is documented here rather than left
  silent.

